[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5337960678","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120461#issuecomment-5337960678","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120461","id":5337960678,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPirQ5g","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T05:34:48Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T05:53:33Z","body":"Imo ideally wherever possible we should avoid NaN at source, rather than attempt to deal with it in runtime code. Where is this NaN coming from?\r\n\r\nIf it is loaded data, we should detect and replace NaN in any loaded data, or outright reject the data, imo.\r\n...\r\n\r\nWith NaNs there's a broader conversation here:\r\nShould NaNs be detected:\r\n\r\n1) At introduction\r\n2) At runtime\r\n\r\nImo we should focus on (1) as much as possible rather than (2). Anytime we see a NaN we should try and debug and find where it comes from, and close that problem ideally.\r\n\r\nFor (2) it has the potential to be a big downside, so should ideally be limited to specific high traffic areas.\r\n\r\n(2) obviously creates a lot of safety code to write / debug / read, it ruins CPU pipelining / branch prediction / performance in tight loops.\r\n\r\n(2) also often introduces silent failure, hiding an underlying bug, making it harder to track down.\r\n\r\nThere's often an exception for checking NaN in shaders, where checking for NaN / divide by zero is expensive, and GPUs are designed to deal with it gracefully anyway.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5337960678/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5338263538","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120461#issuecomment-5338263538","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120461","id":5338263538,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPi9v8g","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T06:12:41Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T06:14:22Z","body":"@lawnjelly https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120461/changes#r3460637476\r\n\r\nAs Jolt's comment there states, although it isn't documented, the height map implicitly treats holes as NaN. In this case, should we change the specifications for the height map? Then modules that rely on that implicit NaN might break.\r\n\r\n> Godot has undocumented (accidental?) support for holes by passing NaN as the height value, whereas Jolt uses FLT_MAX instead, so we translate any NaN to FLT_MAX in order to be drop-in compatible.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5338263538/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5338798825","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120461#issuecomment-5338798825","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120461","id":5338798825,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABPjea6Q","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-19T07:16:39Z","updated_at":"2026-08-19T07:18:41Z","body":"Awk, that's pretty messy, but I guess hold our noses. :grin: \r\n\r\nIs this `_heightmap_cell_cull_segment()` a hot path?\r\n\r\nIf so it might be worth pre-marking the face as a hole, and / or better yet create a list of non-hole faces for testing. Presuming that it is tested more often than it is created.\r\n\r\nIf it's not a hot path, then the PR is likely fine, but the aliases might make it more readable.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5338798825/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]